<title>UK: Ex-dividends to take 3.35 points off FTSE, Oct 14.</title>
<headline>Ex-dividends to take 3.35 points off FTSE, Oct 14.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following FTSE 100 index stocks will go ex-dividend on October 14 and analysts estimate the effect will be to take 3.35 points off the index that day.</p>
<p>						DIVIDEND    INDEX</p>
<p>						(PENCE)     EFFECT</p>
<p>     COMPANY				 Net   Gross  Gross</p>
<p>* Bank of Scotland			 2.91   3.638  0.254</p>
<p>* British Gas				6.40   8.000  2.064</p>
<p>* Great Universal Stores		11.50  14.375  0.848</p>
<p>* Smith &amp; Nephew			   2.29   2.863  0.186</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7954</p>
</text>
